-- title:
--   Computing one initial graph-sketch cell from cached signs
-- statement:
--   Let cached integers $X$ all be signs, let $v$ be a length-$k$ sign vector, and let headers contain $n,k,u,a$ and $|X|$. Suppose the address $j=nk+an+u$ is valid, its arithmetic expression and relevant counters fit width $w\ge1$, the depth has $k$ markers, and the lookup and wedge helpers are empty. The first-cell program increments $a$ and prepends the marked array
--   $$X_j\operatorname{wedgeReverse}(v,U_k),\qquad t\le10^7(w+k+2)^2 2^k+10000(|X|+1).$$
--   The cached signs, labels, other registers and tails are restored. This is the native implementation of one first-layer sketch state at a vertex.
-- source:
